\description{
\strong{Get the header of one game from the live API: teams, codes, coaches, score
by quarter, venue, referees, one row.}

Endpoint: \verb{GET https://live.euroleague.net/api/Header?gamecode=\{game_code\}&seasoncode=\{season_code\}}

The header is a flat object: teams, codes, coaches, the score and the
\strong{cumulative} score at the end of each quarter (\code{score_quarter1_a} ...),
venue, capacity (as reported; its semantics are unverified) and referees.
Team A is the home side as measured on one game.
}
\details{
Unofficial, keyless API, not supported by Euroleague Basketball; hoopR only
wraps it (wrap-only: payloads are not redistributed as release assets). This
function mirrors its sdv-py twin of the same name: same arguments, defaults
and snake_case columns, one row per sdv-py row.

The live API's codes are space-padded fixed-width strings
(\code{TEAM = "IST       "}); every string cell is stripped. Its "no such game"
answer is an \strong{empty 200 body}, returned as a zero-row tibble with the
documented columns (not an error). A 404 raises \code{hoopR_no_data}, a 400 / 422
\code{hoopR_invalid_request}, any other failure \code{hoopR_fetch_error} (all inherit
\code{hoopR_error}).
}
